From: Chris Scott <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: refresh the tx BA session timer on NPU devices

NPU-forwarded frames bypass the software TX path that refreshes last_tx.
Include active NPU devices in the existing WED TX status refresh condition
so negotiated nonzero BA timers do not expire during offloaded transfers.

Adapted to the local b2704cf5 + NPU patch stack; no behavior changes from
the author's 2026-09-18 submission. Submission is not claimed as merged.
Source: https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/09/18/1149
Message-ID: <20260918091659.1176350-1-gilroyscott@hotmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Chris Scott <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>


--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1381,7 +1381,8 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed) && wcid->sta) {
+	if ((mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed) ||
+	     mt76_npu_device_active(&dev->mt76)) && wcid->sta) {
 		struct ieee80211_sta *sta;
 		u8 tid;
 
